{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "002M", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{J}$", "MATH_0003": "$M : \\mathcal{I} \\times \\mathcal{J} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$M_{i, \\infty} = \\colim_j M_{i,j}$", "MATH_0005": "$i$", "MATH_0006": "$M_{-, \\infty} : \\mathcal{I} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0007": "$M$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{categories-lemma-colimits-commute}\n", "suffix": "\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0a82681bea7b714709f4dae0e27a36ad5ccbe7188dda92d2b9a1cff676fbcc6a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:82baa79b9cbcabf0a679973c19a9a64892c4a0b5fe645611caa4f1c3f231a0f4", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>, <MATH_0002> be index categories. Let <MATH_0003> be a functor. Assume that <MATH_0004> exists for all <MATH_0005>. Then the resulting functor <MATH_0006> has a colimit if and only if <MATH_0007> does, and then the colimits coincide. In particular, we have", "source_text_hash": "sha256:92a550181d4ec788201c2cd92a9998f0f72a082e98afd16e5eee4c20794dafd5", "unit_id": "tag:002M:statement"}
